    },
    "discover_ayurveda_section_gnHETK": {
      "type": "discover-ayurveda-section",
      "blocks": {
        "ayurveda_item_UywwNH": {
          "type": "ayurveda_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "description": "<p>Ayurveda, derived from the Sanskrit words “Ayur” (life) and “Veda” (Knowledge), translates to “the knowledge of life.”It is India’s ancient system of natural healing — one that recognizes every individual as unique, and every imbalance as an opportunity for restoration.<br/>Where Western beauty routines focus on correction, Ayurveda focuses on connection — between the mind, body, and spirit. It teaches that true radiance cannot be achieved through products alone, but through mindful ritual, nourishment, and alignment with nature’s rhythm.<br/>Every sunrise and sunset, every season, every breath we take is considered part of this divine balance. And when that balance is restored, the glow of the skin becomes the outer expression of inner wellness — your Prana.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ayurveda_item_UywwNH"
      ],
      "name": "What Is Ayurveda?",
      "settings": {
        "subheading": "",
        "heading": "What Is Ayurveda?",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Rectangle_10_5.png",
        "desktop_layout": "image_first",
        "mobile_layout": "image_first"
      }
    },
    "doshas_philosophy_section_Th84wH": {
      "type": "doshas-philosophy-section",
      "blocks": {
        "dosha_item_xk8BHj": {
          "type": "dosha_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/image_5.webp",
            "title": "Vata (Air + Ether)",
            "description": "<p>The dosha of movement and creativity. When balanced, it brings lightness and inspiration; when imbalanced, it can cause dryness or dullness in the skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "dosha_item_yNd8CJ": {
          "type": "dosha_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/image_6.avif",
            "title": "Pitta (Fire + Water)",
            "description": "<p>The dosha of transformation and metabolism. Balanced Pitta radiates warmth and confidence; imbalance may cause redness or sensitivity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "dosha_item_QFGCRQ": {
          "type": "dosha_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/image_7.webp",
            "title": "Kapha (Earth + Water)",
            "description": "<p>The dosha of stability and nourishment. In balance, it brings soft, hydrated skin and emotional grounding; in excess, it can lead to congestion or sluggishness.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "dosha_item_xk8BHj",
        "dosha_item_yNd8CJ",
        "dosha_item_QFGCRQ"
      ],
      "name": "Three Doshas Philosophy",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "The Philosophy of the Three Doshas",
        "subheading": "According to Ayurveda, all living beings are made up of five elementsair, fire, water, earth, and ether which combine to form three life energiesknown as Doshas:",
        "description": "Understanding your dosha is the foundation of personalized beauty. At Prana Beauty, our AI-powered skin quiz draws inspiration from theseAyurvedic principles — interpreting your skin’s signals to recommendrituals that restore your unique balance."
      }
    },
    "self_care_section_rcW6qF": {
      "type": "self-care-section",
      "name": "Ayurveda Self-Care",
      "settings": {
        "background_image": "shopify://shop_images/Frame_2147225749_1.png",
        "heading": "Ayurveda and Beauty: The Ritual of Self-Care",
        "description": "<p>In Ayurveda, beauty (Saundarya) is not about youth or perfection — it is about Ojas, the radiant life force that glows from within. An Ayurvedic skincare ritual is not rushed or mechanical. It’s intentional, sensual, and deeply personal — a meditation in motion.<br/>Daily rituals might include gentle cleansing with botanicals, applying nourishing oils infused with herbs, and massaging the skin in slow, circular motions to stimulate circulation and awaken energy. Each act of care is an offering — a conversation with your body and spirit.<br/>At Prana Beauty, we preserve these sacred traditions through formulations enriched with Kashmiri saffron, turmeric, sandalwood, bakuchiol, and cold-pressed oils — each ingredient selected for purity, vibrational energy, and skin affinity. Our small-batch process ensures freshness and potency, so your ritual feels as alive as nature itself.</p>"
      }
    },
    "discover_ayurveda_section_Md4WBr": {
      "type": "discover-ayurveda-section",
      "blocks": {
        "ayurveda_item_dpCmAU": {
          "type": "ayurveda_item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "description": "<p>Ayurveda reminds us that no two people — or complexions — are alike. Yet modern skincare often overlooks this individuality.<br/>That’s why we’ve integrated AI-powered personalization into our Ayurvedic foundation.<br/>Through intelligent skin analysis, Prana Beauty translates ancient understanding into modern precision — offering rituals that are both timeless and tailored. Our technology helps you discover which botanicals align with your dosha and skin type, ensuring every drop you apply works in harmony with your body’s natural intelligence.<br/>This synthesis of heritage and high performance is what defines modern Ayurveda — skincare that is both rooted in wisdom and elevated by innovation.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
