        "ingredient_NXUXr6": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Kashmir Saffron",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Saffron",
            "botanical": "Crocus sativus flower extract",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/saffron_strands_4623abde-e272-40e5-af42-cddae80b25aa.png",
            "description": "Kashmir Saffron — Kumkuma in Sanskrit — is the most potent brightening\ningredient in Ayurvedic skincare. Crocin and crocetin, its active carotenoids,\ninhibit tyrosinase and reduce melanin synthesis at the cellular level. It has\nbeen used in Ayurvedic skincare formulations for over 4,000 years. PRANA\nsources exclusively from the Pampore region of Kashmir — the only terroir\nthat produces saffron with sufficient crocin concentration to deliver\nmeasurable brightening results in a topical formula.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Brightening Mechanism",
            "accordion_1_content": "Crocin inhibits tyrosinase — the enzyme that converts tyrosine into\nmelanin reducing pigmentation at source rather than masking it at\nthe surface.",
            "accordion_2_title": "Antioxidant Activity",
            "accordion_2_content": "Safranal and picrocrocin neutralise free radicals generated by UV and environmental pollution, protecting against oxidative stress that accelerates pigmentation and ageing.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Circulation & Glow",
            "accordion_3_content": "Saffron improves microcirculation to skin tissues, increasing oxygen delivery — the physiological basis of the luminosity associated with Kumkuma rituals in Ayurvedic practice.",
            "accordion_4_title": "Anti-inflammatory",
            "accordion_4_content": "Crocetin modulates inflammatory cytokines, reducing post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation — the most common form of uneven skin tone in South Asian and deeper skin tones.",
            "product_1": "Saffron Glow Face Oil",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "Saffron Radiance Moisturizer",
            "product_2_url": "",
            "product_3": "Bakuchiol Night Restorative Serum",
            "product_3_url": ""
          }
        },
        "ingredient_WX7678": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Bakuchiol ",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Bakuchiol",
            "botanical": "Psoralea Corylifolia Seed Oil",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Bakuchiol_1.png",
            "description": "Bakuchiol is the plant-derived answer to the retinol question. Extracted from the seeds of the babchi plant — Psoralea Corylifolia — it has been used in Ayurvedic medicine for centuries and is now the subject of significant clinical research. Multiple peer-reviewed studies confirm Bakuchiol stimulates retinol-like gene expression: upregulating collagen synthesis, increasing cellular turnover, and reducing the appearance of fine lines and hyperpigmentation — without retinol's photosensitivity, irritation, barrier disruption, or pregnancy contraindications. It can be used morning and evening. It does not require gradual introduction. It is safe for all skin types including sensitive. In Ayurveda it is classified under Rasayana herbs — substances that promote longevity and tissue renewal.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Retinol-Equivalent Action",
            "accordion_1_content": "Bakuchiol activates retinol receptor pathways (RAR and RXR) without being structurally related to retinol — achieving cell turnover stimulation via a different molecular route.",
            "accordion_2_title": "Collagen Synthesis",
            "accordion_2_content": "Upregulates Type I, III, and IV collagen gene expression — the structural proteins responsible for skin firmness and elasticity that decline with age and UV exposure.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Zero Irritation",
            "accordion_3_content": "Unlike retinol, bakuchiol does not trigger TRPV1 receptor activation — the pathway responsible for the redness, peeling, and sensitivity associated with retinoid use.",
            "accordion_4_title": "Antioxidant Protection",
            "accordion_4_content": "Potent free radical scavenger — protects against lipid peroxidation and oxidative DNA damage, supporting cellular longevity alongside its renewal action.",
            "product_1": "Bakuchiol Night Restorative Serum",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "",
            "product_2_url": "",
            "product_3": "",
            "product_3_url": ""
          }
        },
        "ingredient_EzCGMH": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Turmeric Root Extract",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Turmeric",
            "botanical": "Curcuma Longa Root Extract",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Turmeirc_18463052-bc95-4d90-b93d-c1204ed175e5.png",
            "description": "Turmeric is classified in Ayurvedic medicine as a Varnya herb — a botanical whose primary therapeutic action is to bring luminosity and clarity to the complexion. Its mechanism of action on skin is precise and well-documented: curcumin inhibits tyrosinase (the enzyme that drives melanin synthesis, producing dark spots and uneven tone), suppresses cyclooxygenase-2 inflammatory pathways that cause post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, and provides antioxidant protection during the mask period. The Ubtan ritual — turmeric paste applied to the skin before bathing — has been documented in Ayurvedic texts for over 3,000 years. It was prescribed for brides the night before marriage specifically for this brightening, clarifying action.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Melanin Inhibition",
            "accordion_1_content": "Curcumin inhibits tyrosinase and downregulates MITF — the master transcription factor controlling melanin production — addressing hyperpigmentation at multiple points in the pathway.",
            "accordion_2_title": "Anti-inflammatory",
            "accordion_2_content": "Curcumin suppresses NF-κB — the master inflammatory switch — reducing the cascade that triggers post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation, the most common pigmentation concern in South Asian skin.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Antioxidant",
            "accordion_3_content": "ORAC value of 127,068 — one of the highest of any plant-derived compound. Neutralises free radicals from UV, pollution, and metabolic processes.",
            "accordion_4_title": "Purification",
            "accordion_4_content": "Antimicrobial action against P. acnes and Staphylococcus aureus — supporting clarity without disrupting the skin microbiome.",
            "product_1": "Turmeric & Sandalwood Purifying Mask",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "Saffron Glow Face Oil",
            "product_2_url": "",
            "product_3": "",
            "product_3_url": ""
          }
        },
        "ingredient_4Y44We": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Rose",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Rose",
            "botanical": "Rosa Damascena Flower Extract / Oil",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Rosa_Damascena_Flower_Oil_03a2bb0f-27fc-4006-a176-cca09d41c1e4.png",
            "description": "Rosa Damascena — the Damask Rose — is one of the most valued botanicals in both Ayurvedic and classical perfumery traditions. Its flower oil contains geraniol, citronellol, and nerol — compounds with documented anti-inflammatory and skin-soothing properties that calm post-mask sensitivity. In the mask formula, Rosa Damascena plays a dual role: active soothing agent and ceremonial scent. Alongside sandalwood, it transforms the rinsing step. In Ayurveda, rose is classified as a Pitta-pacifying herb — cooling, calming, and restoring balance to inflamed or sensitive skin.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Skin Barrier",
            "accordion_1_content": "Geraniol and citronellol — the dominant terpenes in Damask Rose — support ceramide synthesis and reinforce the skin's lipid barrier, reducing transepidermal water loss.",
            "accordion_2_title": "pH Balancing",
            "accordion_2_content": "True rose water has a pH of 5.0–5.5 — matching the skin's ideal acid mantle. It restores pH after cleansing and prepares skin to absorb subsequent actives.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Anti-inflammatory",
            "accordion_3_content": "Flavonoids including quercetin and kaempferol inhibit COX-2 enzymes, reducing skin redness and reactivity associated with sensitised skin.",
            "accordion_4_title": "Astringent & Toning",
            "accordion_4_content": "Tannins in the flower extract provide gentle astringency — tightening pores and reducing excess sebum without stripping natural oils.",
            "product_1": "Rose Jasmine Milk Cleanser",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "Pure Rose Water Toning Mist",
            "product_2_url": "",
            "product_3": "",
            "product_3_url": ""
          }
        },
        "ingredient_Ld6mQK": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Sandalwood Oil",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Sandalwood",
            "botanical": "Santalum Album Oil",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/sandalwood_1.png",
            "description": "True Indian sandalwood — Chandan — takes between 15 and 60 years to reach medicinal grade. Santalum album from Mysore is the only variety with documented clinical biocompatibility for skin application. Alpha- and beta-santalol are clinically documented as antimicrobial, anti-inflammatory, and antiseptic. In Ayurveda, sandalwood is a Pitta herb: cooling, calming, the correct botanical response to the heat of active inflammation and post-mask sensitivity. After the three clays have drawn and purified, sandalwood oil cools and tones the skin during the rinse — converting a functional step into a ceremonial one. Its scent is described in Ayurvedic texts as the fragrance closest to the divine.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Anti-inflammatory",
            "accordion_1_content": "Alpha-santalol significantly inhibits COX-2 — a key enzyme in the inflammatory cascade — reducing skin redness and reactive conditions.",
            "accordion_2_title": "Tyrosinase Inhibition",
            "accordion_2_content": "Demonstrated tyrosinase inhibitory activity in vitro, contributing to brightening when combined with saffron and turmeric in PRANA's mask formula.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Antimicrobial",
            "accordion_3_content": "Effective against Staphylococcus aureus, Propionibacterium acnes, and Candida albicans — supporting clear skin without microbiome disruption.",
            "accordion_4_title": "Skin Texture",
            "accordion_4_content": "Alpha-santalol promotes keratinocyte differentiation — supporting smooth, even skin texture and refined appearance.",
            "product_1": "Turmeric & Sandalwood Purifying Mask",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "Saffron Glow Face Oil",
            "product_2_url": "",
            "product_3": "",
            "product_3_url": ""
          }
        },
        "ingredient_bzLA3M": {
          "type": "ingredient",
          "name": "Jasmine",
          "settings": {
            "name": "Jasmine",
            "botanical": "Jasminum Officinale Flower Extract",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Jasmine_Flower_Oil_c3382c05-19f6-447f-a86d-fae0dbefdc89.png",
            "description": "The fragrance system of the Rose Jasmine Milk Cleanser is four natural botanicals: Jasmine (Jasminum Officinale), Narcissus (Narcissus Poeticus), Vetiver (Vetiveria Zizanoides), and Cumin seed (Cuminum Cyminum). No synthetic parfum. No synthetic accords. No isolated aroma chemicals. Jasmine is the top note — warm, floral, deeply associated with Ayurvedic ritual and South Asian ceremonial preparation. Narcissus adds a cool green depth. Vetiver root grounds the blend with its characteristic earthy warmth. Cumin seed adds the unexpected spiced note that makes the scent distinctly Indian rather than generically floral. Together they create the olfactory opening of the PRANA ritual — the signal to the nervous system that the ceremony has begun.",
            "accordion_1_title": "Skin Conditioning",
            "accordion_1_content": "Benzyl acetate and jasmone act as emollients — softening and smoothing the skin surface without occlusive heaviness.",
            "accordion_2_title": "Mild Antiseptic",
            "accordion_2_content": "Jasmine extract demonstrates mild antimicrobial activity against common skin pathogens, supporting skin clarity in the cleansing ritual.",
            "accordion_3_title": "Psychodermatology",
            "accordion_3_content": "Jasmine aroma has documented effects on the limbic system — reducing cortisol and promoting calm alertness. In morning skincare ritual, this creates a measurable psychological benefit alongside the topical one.",
            "accordion_4_title": "",
            "accordion_4_content": "",
            "product_1": "Rose Jasmine Milk Cleanser",
            "product_1_url": "",
            "product_2": "",
